<title>USA: Bristol Technology revises terms.</title>
<headline>Bristol Technology revises terms.</headline>
<dateline>NEWPORT BEACH, Calif. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bristol Technology Systems Inc and Smyth Systems Inc said they have revised terms of a previously announced proposed transaction between the two companies.</p>
<p>The revised terms call for Smyth to be acquired by Bristol for an undisclosed amount of cash and stock, the company said.</p>
<p>Previously, the companies had agreed to merge in an exchange of stock to be accounted for on a pooling of interest basis.  Shareholders of Smyth have voted in favor of the revised terms.  The company said it expects the acquisition to close tomorrow.</p>
</text>
